Here are some additional features that can help prevent form spoofing:

**Implementing a One-Time Password (OTP) system**

```html
<!-- Generate an OTP and display it to the user -->
<p>Enter your OTP: <input type="text" id="otp" name="otp"></p>

<!-- Validate the OTP on the server-side -->
if ($_POST['otp'] !== $_SESSION['otp']) {
    // Invalid OTP, handle accordingly
}
```

**Using a secure token or hash to prevent tampering**

```html
<!-- Generate a secure token and store it in a session variable -->
<?php $token = bin2hex(random_bytes(32)); ?>
<input type="hidden" name="_csrf_token" value="<?php echo $token; ?>">

<!-- Validate the token on the server-side -->
if ($_POST['_csrf_token'] !== $_SESSION['csrf_token']) {
    // CSRF protection failed, handle accordingly
}
```

**Implementing a rate limiting system to prevent brute-force attacks**

```html
// Store the IP address and timestamp of each form submission in a database
<?php $ip = $_SERVER['REMOTE_ADDR']; ?>
<?php $timestamp = time(); ?>
INSERT INTO ip_log (ip, timestamp) VALUES ('<?=$ip?>', <?=$timestamp?>);

// Check if the IP has exceeded the allowed rate
if (count(ip_log()) > 10 && time() - max(timestamp) < 60) {
    // Rate limit exceeded, handle accordingly
}
```

**Displaying a CAPTCHA to prevent automated form submissions**

```html
<!-- Display a CAPTCHA image and input field -->
<p>Enter the code: <img src="https://www.globalbank.com/captcha.jpg" alt="CAPTCHA">
<input type="text" id="captcha" name="captcha"></p>

<!-- Validate the CAPTCHA on the server-side -->
if ($_POST['captcha'] !== $_SESSION['captcha']) {
    // Invalid CAPTCHA, handle accordingly
}
```

These features can help prevent form spoofing and ensure that only legitimate users can submit forms.
